          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "しつど (shitsudo) is Sino-Japanese (kango): two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are shitsu, \"damp\" (Middle Chinese syip) and do, \"degrees\" (duH) (KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
            }
          ]
        },
